       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 30 mg is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses that high raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and shock. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the usual maximum.\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, the typical starting dose. It can be titrated up after 1\u20132 weeks.\n- **2.5 mg PO once daily**, which is used for frail or elderly patients, or in hepatic impairment.\n\nIf 30 mg is intentional, for example as part of a specific protocol, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting the rationale. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
